<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>MedUI: set up this computer</title>
<style>
  :root { --bg:#f6f7f9; --card:#fff; --text:#1d2330; --muted:#5b6576; --accent:#1f6feb; --ok:#1a7f37; --line:#d8dde5; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --bg:#14171c; --card:#1d2128; --text:#e6e9ee; --muted:#9aa4b2; --accent:#58a6ff; --ok:#3fb950; --line:#2f3540; }
  }
  body { margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--text); font:15px/1.55 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; }
  main { max-width:640px; margin:2.5rem auto; padding:0 16px; }
  .card { background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:10px; padding:1.4rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom:1rem; }
  h1 { font-size:1.35rem; margin:0 0 .4rem; }
  h2 { font-size:1rem; margin:0 0 .5rem; }
  p, li { color:var(--muted); }
  .btn { display:inline-block; background:var(--accent); color:#fff; text-decoration:none; padding:.6rem 1.1rem; border-radius:7px; font-weight:600; }
  code, .thumb { font-family:ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; font-size:.9em; }
  .thumb { display:block; word-break:break-all; background:var(--bg); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; padding:.5rem .7rem; color:var(--text); margin:.4rem 0 .2rem; }
  #checking { color:var(--muted); }
  #trusted { display:none; color:var(--ok); font-weight:600; }
  #setup { display:none; }
  ol { padding-left:1.2rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <div class="card">
    <h1>MedUI</h1>
    <p id="checking">Checking whether this computer is set up…</p>
    <p id="trusted">This computer is set up. Opening MedUI…</p>
    <div id="setup">
      <p>MedUI runs on this practice's own network and uses a certificate from the practice, so
         each computer needs to trust it once. After that, MedUI opens at
         <a href="@@URL@@"><code>@@URL@@</code></a> with a padlock, and the microphone works.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="windows" style="display:none">
    <h2>Windows</h2>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/setup-medui.cmd" download>Download the setup for this PC</a></p>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the downloaded <code>setup-medui.cmd</code>. If Windows says it protected your PC, choose
          <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>.</li>
      <li>Approve the administrator prompt (to set up MedUI for everyone who uses this PC). Without
          approval it sets up only your own Windows account.</li>
      <li>Check the thumbprint it shows against the one below, then answer <em>y</em>.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="check" style="display:none">
    <h2>Check before you trust it</h2>
    <p>The certificate's thumbprint. It should match what your IT or practice manager has (it was
       shown when MedUI was set up). If it doesn't, stop and ask them.</p>
    <span class="thumb">@@THUMB@@</span>
    <p>It may only vouch for: <code>@@NAMES@@</code>. It can't be used for any other website.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="other" style="display:none">
    <h2>Other computers and browsers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Firefox:</strong> after the Windows setup, set <code>security.enterprise_roots.enabled</code>
          to <code>true</code> in <code>about:config</code>, or import the certificate in Firefox's settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Mac:</strong> download <a href="/medui-root.cer">the certificate</a>, open it in Keychain Access,
          add it to the System keychain and set it to <em>Always Trust</em>.</li>
      <li><strong>iPad or iPhone:</strong> download <a href="/medui-root.cer">the certificate</a>, install the profile in
          Settings, then turn on full trust in <em>General › About › Certificate Trust Settings</em>.</li>
      <li><strong>Practices with a Windows domain:</strong> IT can trust it for every PC at once with Group Policy.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</main>
<script>
// Reaching MedUI over HTTPS only succeeds once this computer trusts the certificate; an
// untrusted certificate makes the request fail. Then go straight on to MedUI.
(function () {
  var target = '@@URL@@';
  var show = function (id) { document.getElementById(id).style.display = 'block'; };
  var hide = function (id) { document.getElementById(id).style.display = 'none'; };
  var setup = function () { hide('checking'); ['setup', 'windows', 'check', 'other'].forEach(show); };
  var timer = setTimeout(setup, 6000);
  fetch(target + '/health', { mode: 'no-cors', cache: 'no-store' })
    .then(function () { clearTimeout(timer); hide('checking'); show('trusted'); location.replace(target + '/'); })
    .catch(function () { clearTimeout(timer); setup(); });
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
